# Every file is checked out byte-for-byte. `* -text` turns off line-ending
# conversion for the whole tree, and it is here for one reason: a Windows
# checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites every `.ax` source and every
# `.out` golden to CRLF, and then every byte-comparing gate in the
# repository - the stdlib goldens, the formatter parity cases, the
# self-hosting fixpoint - goes red at once for a reason that has nothing
# to do with the compiler. The emitter writes `\n` and only `\n`, and the
# goldens compare bytes, so the checkout has to be bytes too. Added ahead
# of the first Windows CI leg rather than the morning after it.
* -text
